<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Binnya Dala</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1774</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Binnya Dala was the last king of the Restored Hanthawaddy Kingdom of the Mon in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-burma">Lower Burma</a>, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bago">Pegu</a> from 1747. With French help he built up an army and in 1752 captured Ava, ending the Toungoo dynasty. The Burman leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaungpaya">Alaungpaya</a> then reconquered the country and took Pegu in 1757. Binnya Dala was held captive and executed in 1774.</p></div>
